second baseman of modern times? It was in the Fifties when I managed at Denver and had Weaver with me.
“Branch Rickey called men one day and told me I was being moved from Denver to New Orleans as manager and
that he had a young second baseman he wanted me to take ‘and teach. “You were a second baseman,’ he told me, ‘and I
