Mr. Rickey argued, So did I. It very probably was the first and only time Mr, Rickey ever relented, But I insisted on
Weaver because he could do so many more things than play second base. And I told Mr. Rickey that,
“Well, Mr. Rickey was very perturbed, But he agreed to Jet me have Weaver at New Orleans. He skipped the other
boy to Williamsport in the Eastern League. He did turn out to be a good one (the other “ballplayer was Bill Mazeroski).
