COHEN, BEJMA TO PLAY IN OLD-TIMERS GAME
Andy Cohen and Ollie Bejma, two longtime, popular second basemen of Twin Cities professional baseball, will
be in the starting lineups of the second annual Saints-Millers Old-Timers Game at Metropolitan Stadium, Tuesday, July 16.
Cohen, who played for the Millers from 1932 to 1939 and saw service with the New York Giants in 1926-28-29, is
now baseball coach of the University of Texas-El Paso as well as of El Paso in the Texas League.
Bejma, the American Association’s Most Valuable Player in 1938 while a member of the Saints and now an Indiana state employe, also played with St. Paul Cohen in 1940-41. Bejma played for the St. Louis Browns from 1934 through 1936 and with the Chicago White Sox in 1939.
Also among the 30 Old-Timers accepting bids were Gene Kelly, Saints’ pitcher in 1945-46 who is now Bloom-
ington recreation director, and Lefty Johnson, a Miller hurler-outficider in 1943 who is now employed as a bar-
tender in Minneapoiis.
Boston Red Sox manager Dick Williams, a 1954 Saint, and Boston coach Eclie Popowski, the Millers’ last
manager in 1960, wil! he playing managers of the squads which will play a one-hour or three-inning game before
the Boston-Minnesota Twins game.


